Third-party work
----------------

Miuix - https://github.com/compose-miuix-ui/miuix
  Copyright 2024-2026 compose-miuix-ui contributors. Licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
  Since Hwallet 1.7.4 / Kwallet 3.97.4 the "Miuix" UI style (Settings > UI style) recreates
  Miuix component metrics (cards, list rows, buttons, text fields, switches, dialogs, bottom
  sheets, navigation bar, snackbars) in CSS, and the pull-to-refresh indicator ports the math of
  PullToRefresh.kt and SpringUtils.kt (damping curve, thresholds, spring, capsule drawing) to
  JavaScript (hwallet/web) and Kotlin (HwPull.kt). No Miuix binaries or fonts are bundled.

Material Design 3 - https://m3.material.io
  The "Material UI" style follows the public Material 3 specification and the token values of
  androidx.compose.material3 (Apache License 2.0, The Android Open Source Project).
Gem Wallet - https://github.com/gemwalletcom/wallet
  Copyright (C) Gem Wallet contributors. Licensed under GPL-3.0.
  Hwallet's layout and components (asset lists and rows, chain badges, bottom
  navigation, send/receive and network pickers, activity feed, settings structure)
  and wallet logic (per-chain history parsing, token metadata sources, explorer links)
  follow Gem Wallet. Since Hwallet 1.3 the home header (centred wallet chip, scan and
  search) and the round Send / Receive buttons copy Gem's layout, with Gem's Material
  Symbols icons (send, QR code, QR scanner, search, chevron; Apache-2.0 by Google, as
  shipped in Gem Wallet android/ui). Gem Wallet's name and logo are not used. Gem Wallet is not
  affiliated with Hwallet.

Gem Wallet assets - https://github.com/gemwalletcom/assets (fork of trustwallet/assets)
  Copyright (c) 2019-2023 Trust Wallet. Licensed under the MIT License.
  Chain and token logos bundled in hwallet/web/index.html and loaded from
  assets.gemwallet.com.

Monero symbol - The Monero Project, https://getmonero.org/press-kit/

Kwallet (the offline signer in app/ and web/) is a separate program under the MIT
License (see ../LICENSE). It talks to Hwallet only through Android intents.

v1.5 scanner: QR decoding by ZXing core (https://github.com/zxing/zxing, Apache-2.0) and camera by AndroidX CameraX
(Apache-2.0). Scanner layout follows Gem Wallet (GPL-3.0). No Google Play services code scanner is used.

WalletConnect (v1.6): Hwallet bundles Reown WalletKit 1.6.0 and @walletconnect/core / utils 2.26.0
(Apache License 2.0, github.com/reown-com/walletkit and github.com/WalletConnect/walletconnect-monorepo) and their
MIT-licensed dependencies (@noble/*, @scure/*, ox, es-toolkit and others), inlined offline into web/index.html.
The relay socket is native; the Reown project ID is filled on the phone and never reaches the page.

